Z||000006||MontanaFiero||04-15-2001||04:07 AM||||Wait... AHHHGG-- now I'm really confused!! My coupe (85 mph gauge) is lit from the front with a cheesy orange glow. Is that "offset"?  But my '86 SE is lit from BEHIND. Am I to understand that this too is not true backlighting? That now I have to go find a 120mph cluster just to get the effect I want~!?<P>Now I am compelled to take my cluster apart and see how it works. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||05-28-2001||03:42 PM||||NOT TRUE<BR>There are 85 mph's with the back lit guages.<BR>ALL 84-85 had reflective (offset) lighting.<BR>86-88. GT's and SE's have backlit guages.<BR>It is true that all 120's are backlit.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||05-28-2001||04:08 PM||||All 4-cyl gauges are reflector<BR>All v-6 gauges with the exception of '85 are backlit. '85 v-6 gauges are reflector.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jay||05-28-2001||06:11 PM||||84,85= offset<BR>86-88= backlight<BR>I have a 190km/120mph backlight speedo from an 86GT if anyone is interested.  Works fine. E-mail for details<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gangster.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||fiero56||05-28-2001||06:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>84,85= offset<BR>86-88= backlight<BR>I have a 190km/120mph backlight speedo from an 86GT if anyone is interested.  Works fine. E-mail for details<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What I worte above is correct. <P>ALL 4-cyl gauges are reflector, 84,85,86,87,88. ALL v-6 gauges except '85 are backlit, 86,87,88. '85 v-6 gauges are reflector.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jay||05-28-2001||06:50 PM||||Then someone fooled around with the 86 4cyl cluster that I picked out of the wreckers, because it was definately backlight and 85mph.  Sold it in the kit car.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gangster.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||AusFiero||05-29-2001||09:15 AM||||My 86 GT is backlit so I can agree with that it is probably only 120 mph speedos that are.<P>White face gauges can be printed to be backlit using a layers process. I made my own at home printing on stick on laminating film, quality thin paper (to allow light through it. and them more laminating film.<P>The back layer is a blackout layer printed black with your backlit colour printed slightly larger than the lettering etc in front of it, kind of like a halo around the shapes. When printed the coloured sections are translucent.<P>The next layer is paper and has all the gauge face details on it.<P>The last layer is more laminate to get the right thickness to do a total gauge face replacement rather than a sticker.<P>I changed mine to green backlighting but that is a hell of a job to get right as you have switches to consider also. I am still not happy with it as I want more light behind it. Have painted fluro green etc but if I could find a way to set up low voltage fluro lamps instead of bulbs I think it would work well.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/interior02_2.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||fiero56||05-29-2001||06:32 PM||||All 4-cyl gauges are 85mph, and all are reflector.<BR>Beginning with '86, all v-6 gauges were backlit, 120mph as well as 85mph. <BR>All '85 v-6 gauges are reflector, and are also 85mph.||||reg||1
Z||000014||cadaver||05-29-2001||10:29 PM||||Hey 56 maybe just one more time. I think then it will be clear.||||reg||1
